From 8db4f4af4620358d348d0339b5afe678da1407ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:10:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: fix deterministic failures on hub runners (container-mode
 perms, stale snapshots/baselines, tsc heap) [daveey] (#26)

- tests/conftest: pin container detection False at both seams (hermes_constants + hermes_platform.host.runtime); runner containers have /.dockerenv so the product skips chmod and ~25 owner-only mode tests saw 0755/0644
- refresh prompt-surface snapshot (rendered on Linux), docs-drift baseline, desktop locales/_keys.desktop.json
- classify_changes: route hermes_cli/top_level_env.py (imported by main_desktop) to the update suites
- js-tests: NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=4096 for the workspace checks (desktop tsc OOMs at 2 GB)
---
 .github/workflows/js-tests.yml                 |  4 ++++
 scripts/ci/classify_changes.py                 |  1 +
 scripts/ci/docs_drift_baseline.json            | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 tests/conftest.py                              |  2 ++
 tests/fixtures/prompt_surface/surfaces.json    | 18 +++++++++---------
 .../fixtures/prompt_surface/tools/memory.json  |  2 +-
 6 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/js-tests.yml b/.github/workflows/js-tests.yml
index 06e634f0aa..6d29ca8add 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/js-tests.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/js-tests.yml
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@ jobs:
       # not an empty run, because an empty run reports green after it checks
       # nothing.
       - name: Run all workspace checks
+        # apps/desktop's typecheck (several tsc passes over the whole renderer) peaks past node's
+        # default ~2 GB old-space cap and dies with "heap out of memory"; the runners have 10 GB.
+        env:
+          NODE_OPTIONS: --max-old-space-size=4096
         run: node .github/scripts/run-workspace-checks.mjs
       - name: Check the checkout is clean
         # Last step of every job (tests/ci/test_clean_worktree_check.py): a test or CI step that
